    faq: [{"question":"Is my resume saved on a server?","answer":"No. Your resume stays only in your browser tab and never uploads to a server. For example, a 1-page draft with 3 roles and 8 skills wipes on tab shut. You export with local Print to PDF free offline. No account or cloud copy is made."},{"question":"Will the resume pass ATS (applicant tracking systems)?","answer":"It helps a lot but no layout can promise a pass. Standard headings and plain text parse well in most systems. For example, 8 to 10 skills plus 3 roles with dates score cleanly, while images and tables in a 2-page file fail. Keep fonts simple and test with the checker. No upload is needed."},{"question":"What sections and export formats are supported?","answer":"You get summary, experience, education and skills plus instant preview. For example, add 3 roles with 3 bullets each, 1 degree from 2021 and 8 skills, then Print to a clean 1-page PDF like aarav-resume.pdf. Everything builds locally in your browser free offline. No sign-up or upload is required."},{"question":"How do I keep a one-page resume within 400 to 600 words?","answer":"Budget roughly 80 words for header plus summary, 300 words for experience bullets, and 100 words for education alongside skills matrix. Ruthlessly prune antiquated coursework, redundant adverbs, and duplicate tooling mentions after each draft quantification pass. Preview pagination frequently, hyphenating sparingly while preserving accomplishment verbs and numeric proof points intact."},{"question":"Should freshers and experienced candidates structure resumes differently?","answer":"Freshers should elevate internships, capstone builds, olympiad rankings, volunteer leadership, and coursework labs above sparse employment chronology. Veterans conversely foreground promotions, revenue influence, headcount mentored, patents filed, and cross-functional transformations. Both cohorts nevertheless retain single-column chronology, quantified verbs, and mirror posting lexicon for parser compatibility."}],
    howTo: [{"name":"Add your profile","text":"Fill name, headline and 3-line summary, e.g. Aarav Mehta, Frontend Developer, 4 years React, seeking product roles."},{"name":"Add experience","text":"Add two to three roles with metrics, e.g. UI Engineer at Zeta 2022-2025, shipped 12 flows, lifted signup 30%."},{"name":"Add education and skills","text":"Add education plus eight to ten skills, e.g. BSc 2021, TypeScript, Next.js, Figma, tested against posting keywords."},{"name":"Export to PDF","text":"Preview single-column layout, trim to 500 words one page, then Print to PDF e.g. aarav-resume.pdf offline."}],
    guide: [{ heading: "What a clean resume is", body: "A clean resume is a one-page summary of contact, headline, quantified experience, schooling, and eight to ten skills tuned toward applicant tracking parsers. Recruiters spend seconds hunting job titles, dates, metrics, and stack keywords before shortlisting. For example, frontend developer Aarav Mehta shows four years React, three roles, BSc 2021, plus TypeScript and Next.js, scoring above 80% coverage against postings demanding those phrases. Keep total length 400 to 600 words so single page breathes without cramming margins. Experienced hires foreground promotions, budgets, and headcount mentored, while freshers spotlight internships, capstones, certifications, and freelance gigs occupying identical scaffolding. Edge case: graphics-heavy portfolios with icons and text boxes confuse parsers despite human appeal. Limitation: layout alone cannot invent tenure, authorise credentials, or guarantee callbacks. Validate keyword overlap beforehand at /ats-resume-checker." }, { heading: "How to structure a one-page resume", body: "Use headline plus three-sentence summary, two to three roles with three bullets each, degree year, and eight to ten posting keywords mirrored verbatim. For example, Aarav lists UI Engineer at Zeta 2022 to 2025, twelve flows shipped, signup lifted 30%, BSc 2021, TypeScript and Next.js, holding 500 words neatly on one A4 page. Table — Layout | Parser success | Guidance: single-column standard headings | 100% | recommended; two-column text boxes | 40% | avoid; scanned image PDF | 10% | never. Prefer plain fonts, left alignment, month-year dates, and bullet verbs like orchestrated or accelerated. Edge case: career switchers with freelance fragments should cluster engagements under one consultancy banner. Limitation: formatting cannot compensate missing prerequisites or employment discontinuities. Rehearse coverage using /ats-resume-checker before exporting." }, { heading: "Resume worked example: 1 page with 8 skills", body: "Export aarav-resume.pdf via browser Print on A4, then proof margins, widows, and hyperlink behaviour across desktop preview. Experienced template: three roles, quantified wins like twelve flows and 30% signup uplift, degree 2021, ten skills across 520 words. Fresher alternative: one internship, two capstone projects, hackathon finalist mention, certification badges, and eight skills across 430 words, substituting trajectory momentum for tenure depth. Test one-page versus two-page pagination and eight versus twelve skills to observe recruiter skimmability trade-offs. Edge case: overseas applications requiring two pages should still front-load essentials on sheet one. Limitation: builder polishes presentation only, skipping deep grammar audits and role-specific tailoring for fifty postings. Score alignment at /ats-resume-checker, draft outreach at /cover-letter-builder with 250 to 350 words, and See /terms." }]
