    guide: [{ heading: "What a quote is", body: "A quotation presents prospective pricing before commitment, itemizing scope, quantities, unit rates, levies, and grand payable with explicit expiry. A plumbing contractor estimates ten hours at sixty dollars hourly for six hundred dollars, while a stationery vendor lists twenty packs at eight dollars each for one hundred sixty dollars, both requiring client acceptance before procurement. Our formatter assembles QUO-2026-014 dated September 14, 2026 with sequential numbering, supplier branding, and crisp print styling entirely on-device. Include payment milestones, delivery windows, and revision allowances to reduce renegotiation friction across trades. Edge case: post-acceptance scope expansions warrant revised versions rather than overwritten originals, preserving audit trails. This aid organizes presentation solely, without guaranteeing enforceability. Archive duplicates chronologically, label revisions clearly, and track responses diligently for conversion." }, { heading: "How totals, validity and GST terms work", body: "Subtotals multiply quantity by unit price per row, taxation applies once against aggregate, and grand total combines both plus adjustments. For example, six hundred dollars at eighteen percent contributes one hundred eight dollars for seven hundred eight dollars payable on QUO-2026-014, while five hours at sixty dollars yields three hundred dollars plus fifty-four dollars tax for three hundred fifty-four dollars. Stipulate fifteen-day effectiveness and fifty percent mobilization advance to secure scheduling priority. Interstate versus intrastate treatment diverges as tabulated: | Supply | Regime | Levy on Rs 20,000 | Maharashtra local | 9% CGST plus 9% SGST | Rs 1,800 plus Rs 1,800 | Karnataka to Delhi | 18% IGST | Rs 3,600 |. Edge case: mixed-rate bundles require line-wise segregation rather than blended averaging, preventing slab misapplication. Validate HSN codes, confirm place-of-supply codes, and consult accountants before issuance." }, { heading: "Shared flow, worked example and limits", body: "Treat estimates as opening stage of commercial workflow, linking numbers consistently from quote through payment acknowledgment. Buyer approval references QUO-2026-014, subsequent authorization cites PO-1042, invoicing records INV-2026-001, and settlement issues RCP-0231, creating traceable chains for auditors. Preserve PDFs chronologically with dates, customer identities, and tax breakups to expedite year-end reviews. Limitation: templating streamlines arithmetic and layout exclusively, excluding inventory control, ledger posting, statutory filing, or judicial validity for high-value infrastructure tenders. Confirm slab interpretations, validity extensions, and penalty clauses with qualified advisors before circulation. See /terms. Test calculations twice, archive drafts securely, communicate revisions promptly, monitor expiry calendars diligently, and reconcile advances against finals methodically for accuracy. Include contact channels, delivery timelines, warranty notes, and signature blocks to strengthen professionalism considerably." }],
